{"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-batches","title":"Sending batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"]},{"anchor":"Encoding-a-batch","title":"Encoding a batch","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch"]},{"anchor":"Waiting-between-attempts","title":"Waiting between attempts","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff"]},{"anchor":"Sending-requests","title":"Sending requests","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"HTTPDestinations","role":"collection","externalID":"HTTPDestinations","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a destination that posts each batch it receives as one request. The body is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whatever its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" writes for the batch’s records, so events need no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conformance and the wire format is yours. It sends with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by default, or through any "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" you pass."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after the next wait of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","type":"reference"},{"text":": 1 second, doubling up to 60 seconds, unless you pass another. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one is delivered or dropped, so a tracker’s store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps the batch’s records until then. A batch the endpoint answers with any other status, whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request can never be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped, logged and reported on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","type":"reference"},{"text":" as an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracing instrument injects the trace context of the batch’s first record into the request’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"header fields, and "},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this module to send to a server whose format you write yourself. For TraffluentCollector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, give the destination a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for PostHog, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"). To read events inside the app or in a test, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destinations"},{"type":"text","text":") instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","","struct PlansEncoder: BatchEncoder {","    func encode(_ batch: [EventRecord]) -> EncodedBatch {","        let plans = batch.compactMap { ($0.event as? SignedUp)?.plan }","        return EncodedBatch(body: Data(plans.joined(separator: \"\\n\").utf8), contentType: \"text\/plain\")","    }","}","","let server = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: endpointURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder(),","    backoff: ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(2), maximumDelay: .seconds(120)))","let drops = server.dropReports","let watching = Task {","    for await drop in drops {","        print(\"Dropped a batch: \\(drop)\")","    }","}","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: server)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers this destination beside the others, and what a delivery does while a batch is retried."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/InvalidBackoff":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/invalidbackoff","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"InvalidBackoff"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"InvalidBackoff"}],"title":"InvalidBackoff","abstract":[{"text":"The error ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/init(checkedInitialDelay:maximumDelay:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" throws for an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"initial delay that isn’t positive, or a maximum delay less than it.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/exponentialbackoff","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How long "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" waits before each new attempt at a batch that wasn’t delivered:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary exponential backoff, each wait twice the one before, up to a maximum."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff/init(checkedInitialDelay:maximumDelay:)":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A backoff that waits "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checkedInitialDelay"},{"type":"text","text":" before the first retry and doubles each wait"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after it, up to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumDelay"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/exponentialbackoff\/init(checkedinitialdelay:maximumdelay:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/init(checkedInitialDelay:maximumDelay:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"checkedInitialDelay","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumDelay","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations14InvalidBackoffV","text":"InvalidBackoff","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"init(checkedInitialDelay:maximumDelay:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinati